# What it cannot do is notice a record re-quoted and registered NOWHERE. Nothing in
# this file can - registration is opt-in per record, which the header states.
# ── a row id must name EXACTLY ONE row ────────────────────────────────────────
#
# **The same defect as the one this file's break records exist to catch, one layer
# up: a check for AT LEAST ONE where EXACTLY ONE is meant.** `mise run
# replay-anchors` resolves a `REDNESS` id to a row with
# `{record: (target, literal) for record, _, target, literal in ANCHORS}`. A dict
# comprehension keeps the LAST duplicate, so a repeated id silently drops a row and
# the survivor may name a different file in a different crate. The orphan check
# below asserts an id resolves to at least one row and cannot see this at all.
#
# Measured on this list before the fix: 113 rows, **111** distinct ids, `L1` and
