    f"    {len(REDNESS)} of the {len(ANCHORS)} rows carry a WATCHED REPLAY - "
    "`mise run replay-anchors` runs those, and no gate runs it; every other row "
    "is resolution-checked and unreplayed"
)
# ── the three states, and ROWS and BLOCKS are NOT interchangeable ──────────────
#
# **A row cannot be unclassified, because being a row IS the classification**: it is
# in `ANCHORS`, so its anchor is checked, or in `DESCRIBED`, so somebody measured
# that quoting it was impossible. Only a BLOCK can be unclassified. That is why the
# row column has no third entry, and why the block column has no `DESCRIBED` one - a
# `DESCRIBED` row's fourth field is prose rather than a literal, so there is no span
# to match and its block figure does not exist. A dash, where a zero would lie.
#
# The unclassified figure is PRINTED and never swept. Relabelling those blocks as
# deliberately described would make every row assert a deliberateness nobody
# checked - this convention's own failure mode arriving through the fix for it, which
# `DESCRIBED`'s header argues at length. Large and visible is the intended state.
print("    by state, and the two columns are different units:")
print("                     rows  blocks")
print(f"      CHECKED        {len(ANCHORS):5d} {blocks_carrying:7d}")
print(f"      DESCRIBED      {len(DESCRIBED):5d} {'-':>7}   (prose, no literal to match)")
print(f"      UNCLASSIFIED   {'-':>5} {len(marked_blocks) - blocks_carrying:7d}   "
      f"({blocks - blocks_carrying} this walk sees, {blind} it does not)")
